 "standard_text": "Solve word problems in context and explain own solution to problems involving addition and subtraction with answers up to 20.",
 "meta_desc": "Free CAPS Grade 1 maths worksheets: word problems that add, take away and compare, with answers up to 20. 100 questions with memos.",
 "key_big": "Picture the story.",
 "key_sub": "Left means take away.",
 "body_html": "<h2>How to think about it</h2><ul><li>Read the story and picture it.</li><li>Altogether, in total, more: add. Left, gave away, ate: take away.</li><li>How many more? Find the difference.</li><li>Check that your answer makes sense.</li></ul><h2>Examples</h2><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>Sipho has 8 sweets and eats 3. How many are left?</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>8 − 3</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: 5</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><div class='sn-tw'><table class='sn-table'><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>What to do instead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Add or take away</td><td>Left means take away.</td></tr><tr><td>The order</td><td>Take the smaller from the bigger.</td></tr><tr><td>The question</td><td>Read what is asked.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
 "faq": [
  {
   "q": "What is the Foundation Phase?",
   "a": "Grade R to Grade 3 in South African schools. Learners are about 6 to 7 years old in Grade 1."
  },
  {
   "q": "How should Grade 1 learners solve stories?",
   "a": "With drawings, counters and number lines."
  },
  {
   "q": "What is a difference?",
   "a": "How many more one number is than another."
  },
  {
   "q": "Do the answers go above 20?",
   "a": "Not in Grade 1."
  }
